In phyloHessianWrapper.rb, there are two things to generate sth like example/LG+G_ph-ref/bl/branch_out.matrix for julia_bl.jl to read. can u write a simple julia code using Phylo.jl to generate it. There r the following 3 steps, 

first use Rscript parse_tree_seq.R example/sim/tree/unrooted.tre to reorder the tips to get the ref.tre

second, use GEN_BASICS to generate basics
third, GEN_BRANCH to generate the branch_out.matrix


504   # do_bl_my_try.R to generate julia_outdir (basics)
505   cmd = "Rscript #{GEN_BASICS} -s #{seqfile} -t #{out_treefile} --cpu #{cpu} --julia_o    utdir #{outdirs[:basics]} --force --type #{st}"
506   execute_command(cmd, "Generating basic info of the tree and alignment ......")
507 
508   # generate_branch_out_mat.sh
509   cmd = "bash #{GEN_BRANCH} -t #{out_treefile} --ref_tree #{ref_treefile} --outdir #{o    utdirs[:bl]} --force"
510   execute_command(cmd, "Parsing the branch order ......")
